The conventional case: triple-backtick fence, info string is a language identifier, body is source code.

Live:

```js
const sum = (a, b) => a + b;
console.log(sum(2, 3));
```

Source:

````
```js
const sum = (a, b) => a + b;
console.log(sum(2, 3));
```
````

The rendered shape is `<pre class="wltc-md-codeblock wltc"><code class="language-js">…</code></pre>` — marker identity on the outer `<pre>` (so the universal `.wltc` margin lands outside the visible block), the language class on the inner `<code>` (where CSS and syntax highlighters like Prism / highlight.js / Shiki look for it).

